# An inner method sees the data of the enclosing callable, but its write to a bare name changes a local copy, not the
# source (the author 2026-11-11, LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#callable-parts-visibility): inner returns 9, the v of outer
# stays 1, so outer gives 1 * 10 + 9.
fn: outer () int (int: v 1)
    fn: inner () int
        v := 9
        return: v
    end: inner
    int: r inner()
    return: v * 10 + r
end: outer
int: seen outer()
